## ✅ Final Verdict

**VulnChain is an excellent 7th semester ISE major project.** It is NOT "just another project." The approach is validated by published research at IEEE, MIT, and arXiv. The problem is real and urgent. The technical depth goes well beyond typical undergrad work.

### The "selecting repos" concern — addressed:

Selecting repos with transitive vulnerabilities is not "making up results." It's testing your hypothesis where it matters. Every ML paper focuses its evaluation on the scenarios their method is designed to handle. That IS science.

### Honest risks to manage:
1. Narrow MVP to npm only — don't try all 3 ecosystems in v1
2. Get end-to-end pipeline working early — don't wait until week 14
3. Pre-cache demo data — don't rely on live APIs during viva
4. Record a backup demo video — insurance

### Bottom line:
> **This project has strong legs.** Not just academically, but as a genuine contribution to an active research area. Build it with confidence.
